tional Shapley semantics and probability versus logit output scales\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"benchmarks\\\": [\n+    \\\"UCI Statlog (German Credit Data), DOI 10.24432/C5NC77; frozen retained subsets rather than an assumed full-data evaluation\\\",\n+    \\\"ACSIncome-2024-RELSHIPP, derived from Census ACS PUMS and folktables; native RELSHIPP replaces unavailable RELP, so this is not bit-identical to historical ACSIncome\\\",\n+    \\\"Independent zero/affine and feature-permutation controls, not additional public-data benchmarks\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"architectural_shifts\\\": [\n+    \\\"Frozen logistic regression and random forests are the two measured classifier families; there is no supported neural-network or representation-learning comparison\\\",\n+    \\\"Model-agnostic sampled coalition regression gives way to exact leaf-game algebra for exposed forest structure while preserving the fixed probability game\\\",\n+    \\\"Sampled logistic attribution gives way to deterministic probability-scale Fourier/Owen quadrature with rejection and fallback, not to linear logit attribution\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"result_driven_themes\\\": [\n+    \\\"Structure-aware computations improve reference consistency and signed/top-3 agreement in the available evaluations; this is not evidence of higher predictive accuracy\\\",\n+    \\\"Repeatability, endpoint efficiency, top-k agreement, sign agreement, and reference fidelity answer different reliability questions\\\",\n+    \\\"Nonzero uncertainty in numerical reference estimates limits interpretation of residual fidelity gaps; deterministic replay alone does not establish accuracy\\\",\n+    \\\"A sampled-coalition budget is not an equal wall-time budget for structure-aware algebra or quadrature\\\",\n+    \\\"Certificate logic exists in the implementation, but measured acceptance or coverage is not established by the persisted attribution-only outputs\\\",\n+    \\\"Evidence is conditional on fixed background, grouping, model, and output 